    {
      "id": "claim_ac50addd9a3646cb85e8d51c42fd66f3",
      "statement": "Address fallback in vault_http_request is restricted to pre-send connection failures (ConnectTimeout, or a MaxRetryError whose reason is a NewConnectionError) and tries the remaining vetted numeric targets in deterministic order; the per-attempt connect budget is shared across addresses (timeout / len(targets)) while the read timeout stays the full VAULT_TIMEOUT, and a read timeout, reset, or partial response is re-raised without replaying the request on another address.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/vault_transport.py#L74-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:11c306a46786e51762f89797b2dabae63d70f333ea2274a37fdd856e03b6c923:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://doc/vault_transport.md#L34-L38",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0d8e878c4d58d2aa2387169057cd49f100360b0030a10f7120f306642ba8fab9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5e8ee293a05144a98842b741492ee292",
      "statement": "vault_request in billcollector/vault.py implements the shared retry contract with VAULT_TIMEOUT=10 seconds per request and VAULT_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3 total attempts: transient failures (requests.RequestException such as timeouts, and 5xx responses) are retried with a linear delay of VAULT_RETRY_BACKOFF * attempt (2 seconds base); a 4xx response is final and raises VaultAPIError carrying the status code immediately; exhausted attempts raise VaultAPIError without a status; and VaultTransportError is wrapped into a statusless VaultAPIError so configuration/policy failures never retry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://apps/billcollector/vault.py#L28-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b63fd3b4c199da56b245e8186f4c0e1b7afe01f8de1de9eed676a54e38aa77c0:"
        },
